From 84f26e53b0df7189ab98918c38fa59ae876a3c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:54:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: native Dolby Vision enters a dual-mode
 connector in the mode the kernel has

Since 1.0 RC4 native Dolby Vision never started through the HDMI port of an HP ZBook 17 G6
(Quadro RTX 4000), a dual-mode DisplayPort connector that nvidia-drm drives as HDMI (DP-2,
issue #4). There the transport enters only in the mode on the output, with the head turned off and
on (CWinSystemGbm::FlipDVBridgePage()), and that was asked of CDRMAtomic::
IsSelectedModeCommitted(): the selected mode committed, and no modeset pending. A modeset is asked
for also by what changes no mode, and one was pending every time:

 - 15:20:43.522 VideoPlayer changes the mode to 3840x2160 @ 23.976 Hz; on such a connector it is
   not held for the first frame of native output (CModeChangeHold::StartHolds()), so it goes out
   alone (CWinSystemGbm::SetFullScreen(), told 43.789 "OnLostDisplay"): the kernel sets it at
   46.474 s of its clock ("head 3 (HISENSE (DP-2)): 3840x2160, 23.975 Hz, pixel clock 296700 kHz";
   its clock is 2.61 s ahead of kodi.log's, by the turning off and on at 15:20:47.136 = 49.748 s),
   and CCommittedMode records it;
 - 15:20:44.379 the renderer of the video is configured (LinuxRendererGLES::Configure()), which sets
   the colorimetry of its picture: CWinSystemGbm::SetColorimetry() adds the Colorspace property and
   calls SetActive(true), which asks for a modeset;
 - 15:20:44.691 the first frame of native output: IsSelectedModeCommitted() is false for that
   pending modeset ("native Dolby Vision waits: the mode 3840x2160 (296700 kHz) that it would go
   out in is not the one on the output yet"), nothing is committed while native output waits, so
   it stays pending; 15:20:46.733 "native Dolby Vision output disabled: Dolby Vision frames could
   not be shown for two seconds". The same with the second video at 59.94 Hz and every video after.

The entry now asks what the kernel has (CDRMAtomic::SelectedModeOnCrtc(): the CRTC active and its
MODE_ID the selected mode, by timing), and where that cannot be read, what Kodi's commits put there
whatever modeset is pending since (SelectedModeOnOutput()): NVIDIA_DUAL_MODE::EntersInMode(). What
is pending goes out with the entry, which is a modeset in the mode on the output. A change of mode
that is pending, or that the driver refused, still keeps it waiting, and native output still ends
after two seconds of frames there (fail closed). kodi.log says, at the entry, when a pending
modeset goes out with it ("the modeset that is pending changes no mode and goes out with the
entry"), and, where it waits, what the kernel has, what Kodi's commits put there, and whether a
modeset is pending.

An HDMI connector, and every connector of the kernel backends, does not take this way: nothing
changes for them (the RTX 4080 SUPER and the LG C5). The change of mode cannot be held for the
first frame there either: neither CModeChangeHold nor a move of native output into the mode of
the next video (CDVModeMove) takes a connector whose link native output brings up from scratch.

A host test drives a model of CDRMAtomic (its modeset requests and commits) with the real
CCommittedMode and decisions through that sequence: with the headers of 1.0 RC4 native output
waits all of the 48 frames of two seconds, with these it enters with the first; a change of mode
that the driver refused waits, as before; and an HDMI connector enters in place, as before.
On the laptop and its TV: not verified.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp     | 23 +++++++++++++++++++----
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.cpp    | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h      |  4 ++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/NvidiaDualMode.h | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index 624833b..f331970 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -1949,7 +1949,11 @@ bool CWinSystemGbm::FlipDVBridgePage(CDVBridgeState& state,
   if (valid && !restore && !state.TransportLive() && state.CapturedLinkFromScratch() &&
       drm->IsActive())
   {
-    if (!drm->IsSelectedModeCommitted())
+    // (Hades: the mode on the output by what the kernel has, else by what Kodi's commits put there,
+    // whatever modeset is pending since: NVIDIA_DUAL_MODE::EntersInMode())
+    const std::optional<bool> onCrtc = drm->SelectedModeOnCrtc();
+    const bool committed = drm->SelectedModeOnOutput();
+    if (!NVIDIA_DUAL_MODE::EntersInMode(onCrtc, committed))
     {
       inPlace = false;
       if (state.TakeEntryNotice())
@@ -1957,15 +1961,26 @@ bool CWinSystemGbm::FlipDVBridgePage(CDVBridgeState& state,
         const auto* mode = drm->GetSelectedMode();
         CLog::Log(LOGWARNING,
                   "DVBridge: native Dolby Vision waits: the mode {}x{} ({} kHz) that it would go "
-                  "out in is not the one on the output yet (a modeset pending, or one that the "
-                  "driver refused), and on connector {} the transport does not go out with a "
-                  "change of mode",
+                  "out in is not the one on the output yet (a change of mode pending, or one that "
+                  "the driver refused: the kernel {}; Kodi's commits {}; a modeset {}pending), and "
+                  "on connector {} the transport does not go out with a change of mode",
                   mode ? mode->hdisplay : 0, mode ? mode->vdisplay : 0, mode ? mode->clock : 0,
+                  !onCrtc ? "could not be asked" : *onCrtc ? "has it" : "has another mode, or the output off",
+                  committed ? "put it there" : "did not put it there",
+                  drm->ModesetPending() ? "" : "not ",
                   drm->GetConnector() ? drm->GetConnector()->GetName() : "none");
       }
     }
     else if (state.TakeEntryRestart())
     {
+      // (Hades: a modeset pending that changes no mode, the colorimetry of the renderer of the
+      // video among them, goes out with this entry, which is a modeset in the mode on the output)
+      if (drm->ModesetPending())
+        CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+                  "DVBridge: the mode that native Dolby Vision goes out in is the one on the "
+                  "output (the kernel {}); the modeset that is pending changes no mode and goes "
+                  "out with the entry",
+                  !onCrtc ? "could not be asked; Kodi's commits put it there" : "has it");
       drm->SetActive(false);
       const bool off = drm->FlipPageTransactional(stage(false) ? bo : nullptr, true);
       drm->SetActive(true);
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.cpp
index 10ff8ae..8130e24 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.cpp
@@ -842,6 +842,27 @@ bool CDRMAtomic::SupportsAtomicModesetting()
   return atomic;
 }
 
+std::optional<bool> CDRMAtomic::SelectedModeOnCrtc() const
+{
+  if (!m_crtc || !m_mode)
+    return std::nullopt;
+  const auto active = m_crtc->ReadPropertyValue("ACTIVE");
+  const auto blobId = m_crtc->ReadPropertyValue("MODE_ID");
+  if (!active || !blobId)
+    return std::nullopt;
+  if (*active == 0 || *blobId == 0)
+    return false;
+  drmModePropertyBlobPtr blob = drmModeGetPropertyBlob(m_fd, static_cast<uint32_t>(*blobId));
+  if (!blob)
+    return std::nullopt;
+  std::optional<bool> same;
+  if (blob->data && blob->length >= sizeof(drmModeModeInfo))
+    same = CCommittedMode<drmModeModeInfo>::SameTiming(
+        *static_cast<const drmModeModeInfo*>(blob->data), *m_mode);
+  drmModeFreePropertyBlob(blob);
+  return same;
+}
+
 bool CDRMAtomic::SetVideoMode(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res, struct gbm_bo* bo)
 {
   m_need_modeset = true;
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h
index 1b9a411..62acb8d 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h
@@ -75,6 +75,10 @@ public:
   //! Hades: the selected mode is the one that a commit put on the output, whether a modeset is
   //! pending or not: no change of mode is selected (the depth of the link, LinkDepth.h)
   bool SelectedModeOnOutput() const { return m_committedMode.Is(m_mode, false); }
+  //! Hades: what the kernel has now: whether the CRTC is active and its MODE_ID is the selected
+  //! mode, by timing (CCommittedMode::SameTiming()); nullopt where that could not be read. Read
+  //! from the kernel, as any commit, however made, left it
+  std::optional<bool> SelectedModeOnCrtc() const;
   //! Hades: the ioctls of the commits of native output that change nothing but the picture since
   //! the last call (CDVFrameTest): the tests made before them, the ones committed without a test,
   //! and the time of the commits that did not wait for their flip
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/NvidiaDualMode.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/NvidiaDualMode.h
index 0f7d7a5..f8dcabe 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/NvidiaDualMode.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/NvidiaDualMode.h
@@ -54,4 +54,29 @@ inline bool LinkFromScratch(std::string_view type, std::optional<uint64_t> dualM
 {
   return type == "DP" && DrivenAsHdmi(type, dualModeTmds);
 }
+
+/*!
+ * Hades: whether native Dolby Vision enters now on a connector whose link it brings up from
+ * scratch (LinkFromScratch()): only in the mode on the output, never with a change of it.
+ * modeOnCrtc: what the kernel has now (the CRTC active and its MODE_ID the selected mode, by
+ * timing: CDRMAtomic::SelectedModeOnCrtc()), nullopt where it could not be read; modeCommitted:
+ * what Kodi's commits put there (CDRMAtomic::SelectedModeOnOutput(), CCommittedMode), whatever is
+ * pending since. The kernel's word goes first.
+ *
+ * 1.0 RC4 asked instead whether the selected mode was committed and no modeset was pending
+ * (CDRMAtomic::IsSelectedModeCommitted()). A modeset is asked for also by what changes no mode:
+ * the renderer of the video sets the colorimetry of its picture (CWinSystemGbm::SetColorimetry():
+ * the Colorspace property, SetActive(true)) after the change of mode has gone out alone and before
+ * the first frame of native output. While native output waits, nothing else commits: the modeset
+ * stayed pending, the entry waited for good, and native output ended after two seconds of frames,
+ * with every video (issue #4, HP ZBook 17 G6, 1.0 RC4: "native Dolby Vision waits: the mode
+ * 3840x2160 (296700 kHz) that it would go out in is not the one on the output yet", and the
+ * kernel's log has that mode set 0.8 s before). What is pending goes out with the entry, which is
+ * a modeset in the mode on the output. A change of mode that is pending, or that the driver refused
+ * (the kernel has the mode before it), keeps it waiting, as before.
+ */
+inline bool EntersInMode(std::optional<bool> modeOnCrtc, bool modeCommitted)
+{
+  return modeOnCrtc.value_or(modeCommitted);
+}
 } // namespace NVIDIA_DUAL_MODE
-- 
2.53.0

